"""Preparation-only reference oracle for the true_divide tensor overload.

This file is the reference-as-solution candidate observed by the pytest review
probe.  It is injected through the existing formal ``--override`` mechanism, so
the reviewed call sites stay untouched:

* accuracy: ``flag_gems.true_divide(lhs, rhs)`` in
  ``tests/test_true_divide.py::test_true_divide`` and in the
  ``div_tensor``-marked cases of ``tests/test_div.py`` (override key
  ``true_divide``).
* benchmark: ``op_name="true_divide"`` in ``benchmark/test_true_divide.py``,
  whose ``latency_base`` is the native ``torch.ops.aten.true_divide.Tensor``
  (override key ``true_divide``).

Contract of the representative Definition ``true_divide_tensor``
(aten::true_divide.Tensor(Tensor self, Tensor other) -> Tensor): out-of-place
elementwise true division, returns a fresh tensor, keeps aten dtype promotion
and device, does not mutate and does not alias its operands.

The oracle must not import or call the FlagGems candidate; ``torch.true_divide``
is the native ATen implementation and is only reached without ``use_gems()``
dispatch, which is how the reviewed tests and the override benchmark path call
it.
"""

import torch


def run(lhs, rhs):
    """Elementwise true division with native ATen semantics."""
    return torch.true_divide(lhs, rhs)
